From 8f38bb33402f5a2405d4e827186b8f30f169db90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:38:31 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op null guards: loads through a puppet's missing
 components read 0

A co-op puppet (CoopPuppet_*) has no Player component (main+0x82acc0
returns 0) and no component in slot 10. Game code that runs for the
puppet or an item it wears loads through those null pointers. The
emulator reads 0 there; Hookshot and a real Switch fault. Patch 0002's
zero page hides it on Windows; these guards make it unneeded.

a64_lift.py: Lifter.unless ({pc: (condition, C instead)}): a plain
instruction runs only when the condition is false, else the given C
runs. nx2/coop_null_guards.py puts it on 29 loads of main e0f3ccfa
(word and build id checked): the 25 loads through x0 straight after
`bl main+0x82acc0` with no check, main+0x27975f0 (reached from
the call by a tbz that leaves x0 alone), and the slot-10 chain in f_804d84b0
(main+0x4b85e4..ec). A base below 1 MB gives the load's register 0,
what the emulator reads; the first few uses of each are logged. Seen in
logs: main+0x2dceef8 (guest 0x7d8), main+0x26cf2a4 (guest 0xe58),
main+0x4b85e8 (guest 0x20, a player's crash before 0002's page was on).
Link, who has both components, runs as shipped.

Patch 0038 (bow guard) meets main+0x2dceef8 first and takes the game's
own exit there; this guard stays as its backstop. Patch 0002's zero
page (and the module-armed null page) stays too: it covers loads not
listed here.

nx2/fastfp.py: its copy of emit_function (A64_FASTFP, on by default:
what the game's lift runs instead of the kit's) writes the same guard,
and a guarded load joins no fast float run. nx2/chunks.py: Lifter.unless
goes to the emit's new processes (Windows), as 0005's wraps. Both count
each guard written (stats unless_emitted); nx2/lift.py prints 'co-op null
guards: N of M emitted in the lifted C'.

a64_lift.Lifter.unless defaults to an empty read-only mapping for a
lifter made without __init__ (Longshot's tests/test_fastfp_override.py
runs unchanged).

No file under tests/ (the Linux AppImage ships none, so the kit could not
apply it): the tests are oot-remake-multiplayer's tools/hookshot/
null_guards_cases.py, run on the patched source.
